# 5. DEFINITION VERIFICATION — DO THIS RIGOROUSLY

For every load-bearing definition apply the D1–D10 definition tests.

At minimum verify:

### D1 — Existence

Is the mathematical object actually defined?

### D2 — Domain

What is its domain?

### D3 — Codomain

What is its codomain?

### D4 — Typing

Are all arguments and outputs correctly typed?

### D5 — Totality / Partiality

Is the function total or partial?

### D6 — Uniqueness

Does the definition determine a unique object?

### D7 — Non-emptiness

Is the domain or state space guaranteed non-empty?

### D8 — Constructibility

Can the object actually be constructed from available inputs?

### D9 — Computability

Can the defined object actually be computed?

### D10 — Operational observability

Can KnowledgeOS obtain the information required to instantiate it?

If any test fails, record the exact failure.

Do NOT silently repair the definition.

